  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the most informative first experiment is to establish the simplest possible baseline. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the minimal configuration in the search space: it uses the most standard RNA encoder (PCA), the simplest profile setting, and no image or fusion complexity. This gives a clean reference point for RNA-only performance. Knowing this floor is essential before testing whether (a) a better RNA encoder (scvi, scgpt) helps, (b) image modality adds value, (c) multiprofile aggregation improves things, or (d) multimodal fusion is worthwhile. Starting from the simplest baseline ensures that any subsequent gains can be attributed to specific design choices rather than confounded by multiple simultaneous changes. With 9 experiments remaining, this single baseline anchors the entire comparison hierarchy."
}

